description.text:
The profile to use along the direction of blur:

@b;uniform@n	a box-like profile with uniform weighting along the blur vector
@b;gaussian@n	a gaussian profile with a softer fall-off towards the ends of the blur vector.

Apply the motion blur filter to the motion vectors themselves, before using them to blur the image. This smooths out gradients in the motion vectors, resulting in a softer blur between regions with very different motion.

@b;none@n	don't blur the UVs
@b;uniform@n	apply a small uniform blur to soften edges in the UV map
@b;linear@n	apply a linearly-weighted blur to blend between regions with different motion. This has a stronger  effect than the @b;uniform@n option.
